  "worked_solution": "First, let's recall the double-angle formula for sine: \n\n$$\n2\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x=\\operatorname{sin}\u20612x\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=\\frac{\\pi }{6}$ into the above, we get\n\n$$\n2\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(\\frac{\\pi }{6})\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(\\frac{\\pi }{6})=\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{6})=\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(\\frac{\\pi }{3}).\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n4\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(\\frac{\\pi }{6})\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(\\frac{\\pi }{6})=2\\cdot 2\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(\\frac{\\pi }{6})\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(\\frac{\\pi }{6})=2\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(\\frac{\\pi }{3}).\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
